            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You have two ways:\r\n- Manual use of `lua MiniSessions.write(<session file name>)` and `lua MiniSessions.read(<session file name>)` as `SSave` and `SLoad` versions. With this you have to supply manually session file name without any completion. Example: `:lua MiniSessions.write('nvim-convig')`.\r\n- Interactive use with `lua MiniSessions.select(<action name>)`. It is using overridable `vim.ui.select()`. Example: `:lua MiniSessions.select('read')`.\r\n\r\nAs a general principle 'mini.nvim' does not supply any Neovim commands. Each module creates a global Lua object (`MiniSessions` for 'mini.sessions') which can be used with `:lua MiniSessions...`.",
